cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, board design or the technical reports, please cite it as below."
title: "pcbflow: a personal attempt at LLM for EDA — PCB routing engine, design-flow compiler, STM32H743 core board and technical reports (final archive)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhao
    given-names: Danqi
    affiliation: "Heilongjiang Institute of Technology, School of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/chunhuachaolu-art/pcbflow"
keywords:
  - PCB routing
  - electronic design automation
  - large language models
  - LLM for EDA
  - KiCad
  - negative results
  - pre-registration
abstract: >-
  Solo research project asking where a large language model actually helps in a
  PCB routing pipeline. Contains a from-scratch deterministic router (V5 engine),
  a seven-stage KiCad design-flow compiler, an STM32H743 4-layer core board and six
  Chinese technical reports covering about one hundred pre-registered experiment
  batches. Main finding: the LLM is most useful as an evaluator of routing results;
  most other roles produced negative or null results under matched controls.
